From ff998e10c7d444eab549e633893b1d51301165df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: scratch <scratch@invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:22:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: synchronize BSS and associated STA after real
 TX completion

Keep TC4 credit, management TXdone and STA activation as separate evidence.
Drain the acknowledged management submission before admitting host station
state. Capture one SSID from the validated association request and encode
the pinned gen3 legacy BSS/RLM layout independently. Apply BSS information
before requesting associated STA activation, matching the public AIS path.

Wait for returned command credits and the exact pending STA response
(sequence, AP address, STA and BSS). Normalize the received AID and compare
it with mac80211's live callback input. A negative TX status stops the
attempt before another RF or firmware command.

Production-function host fixtures cover successful ordering, independent
waits and both association command failures. The BSS encoder matches 8192
vendor-struct oracle vectors; actual HIF scalar-write fault fixtures pass
with ASan/UBSan. No device test, data path, keys or completed Wi-Fi support
is claimed. No DCO certification is asserted.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c    |  14 ++
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.h    |   4 +
 .../mediatek/mt6797/join-command-submit.h     |   3 +
 .../wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-commands.h  |  47 +++++
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c    | 165 +++++++++++++++++-
